# K03 S6 (Codex K03-UNIFIED-HEAD-IMPLEMENT-20261006-01 S6; docs #declaration-visibility): a method named as a value is
# the method the site sees -- the emission and the walk read the check's resolution (l2_site_method), not a lookup of the
# name alone.  makeGetter's own fn get, which captures nothing, is visible in its host only; named bare where a value is
# received there, above its definition, it is get's call: t is get() = 3, and g, the returned get, gives 3 too.  Exit 7
# when both are 3.
int: hits 0
fn: makeGetter (int: n) fn: () int
    int: t get
    node\hits: node\hits + t + n - 2
    fn: get () int
        return: 3
    return: get
end: makeGetter
fn: check (int: v) int
    return: v + node\hits + 1
end: check
@: g makeGetter(2)
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: check(g()); stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
